x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 variant of a constructor or destructor it writes inline, where cxx1 emits C1 and C2 for every one - the difference implicit-move.nonames records; the destructors here are written inside their classes and the constructors are implicit, so every one meets it. Measured 2026-10-08 with VS clang 19.1.5 for x86_64-linux-gnu: the twelve cxx1-only names are all C1 or D1.
arm64-darwin  B and Mid are abstract, so no complete object of either is ever built and clang emits no C1 for them; cxx1 emits C1 beside C2 for every class it writes a constructor for. Identical behaviour, one unused symbol each. Measured 2026-10-08: __ZN1BC1Ev and __ZN3MidC1Ev are the only differences, x86_64-windows agrees on all 66.
